    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēfectīvus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj. [deficio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>no.</i> III.), <i>imperfect,
				defective</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et abortiva genitura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Val. 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">febris,</span>”
				<i>intermittent fever</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gramm.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina, verba, some of whose forms are wanting,</span>”
				<i>defective</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Charis. 3</span></i>
			.</div>
